                  DIGITAL SIGNS PACT WITH OFFICEMAX
                 LEADING OFFICE PRODUCTS SUPERSTORE


MAYNARD, Mass. -- Oct. 2, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that OfficeMax, Cleveland, Ohio, (NYSE: OMX) one of 
the country's largest and fastest growing office products 
superstores, will carry Digital's Starion line of retail PCs.  
OfficeMax becomes the first office products superstore chain to 
carry Digital's consumer PC line.

     "OfficeMax is a leading provider of brand name office 
products, business machines, electronics, furniture and computer
hardware and software for small and medium-sized businesses, home
office and individual consumers," said Enrico Pesatori, vice 
president and general manager of Digital's Computer Systems 
Division.  "With its aggressive advertising plans and national base
of stores, OfficeMax fits perfectly with our push to increase brand 
awareness."

     OfficeMax has over 425 superstores covering more than 150 
markets in 42 states and Puerto Rico.  The company will sell the 
new Starion line of Pentium PCs Digital recently announced as part 
of its expanded push into the consumer market.  The new systems 
optimize Microsoft's new Windows 95 operating system and are the 
first consumer PCs to offer home theater-quality JBL speakers.  

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
