                  DIGITAL ANNOUNCES AVAILABILITY OF
                      PRIORIS HX 5133 PC SERVER

  
       Enhances Award-Winning Prioris Line with Pentium 133MHz
                          -Based PC Server

 
MAYNARD, Mass., September 19, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the immediate availability of its Prioris HX 5133 
departmental server, the latest addition to its Prioris HX line of 
highly scalable, Pentium symmetric multiprocessing systems that 
recently won PC Magazine's Editor's Choice Award for Departmental 
File Servers.  Available in single- and dual-processor 
configurations, the Prioris HX 5133 system is fully expandable
and integrates a PCI-to-PCI bridge that enables more available PCI 
expansion slots than any other system in its class.  The addition of 
the 133MHz Pentium processor further enhances the high-performance 
options for customers seeking robust, business class PC servers that 
expand as users' needs grow.

     "Digital is committed to quickly matching the Pentium power 
curve with world class PC server products that provide the 
performance, reliability and engineering excellence that are Digital 
hallmarks," said Duane Dickhut, vice president of Digital's Prioris 
PC Server Product Line.  "The robustness of our PC servers - and the 
ease with which they are integrated into the client/server 
environment - are positive proof-points of Digital's continued 
commitment to provide customers with the best return on investment 
for their IT dollars."

     The Prioris HX 5133 PC server is fully optimized to meet 
customers' needs today and in the future with processor, disk and 
memory scalability, achieved through a balanced system architecture. 
It is designed for businesses running network operating systems, 
industry-standard databases and productivity-critical applications. 
The Prioris HX 5133 incorporates high-performance and expandability 
features such as 512KB secondary level write-back cache (standard), 
PCI Fast-Wide SCSI-2 controllers and devices, and Digital's 
PCI-to-PCI bridge technology which provides a total of 6 bus-master 
PCI slots and 6 bus-master EISA slots.

     Digital's Prioris HX 5133 system is a superior departmental 
server for medium to large workgroups.  Ideal for LAN consolidation, 
and in environments where the highest degree of confidence in data 
integrity is mandatory, the high performance Prioris HX 5133 
delivers excellent reliability and fault-tolerant features, such as: 

     - 	Seven hot-swap device bays with multiple levels of PCI RAID 
        support;

     -	Error Correction Code (ECC) memory support to safeguard data 
        integrity;

     -	A second internal 450-watt redundant power supply (optional) 
        supporting automatic failover and current sharing;

     -	Redundant cooling system with automatic failover fans;

     -	Operator Control Panel to display system status messages;

     -	Dual channel hot swap backplane for increased redundancy; 
        and

     -	Remote Server Manager option to maximize system availability 
        and ease of administration.

     Digital's rackmount option, available for all Prioris servers, 
helps minimize the amount of floor space required in IS 
environments.

     The Prioris HX 5133 PC server supports the widest range of 
operating environments, including Windows NT Server 3.5; Novell 
NetWare 3.X, 4.X and Novell UnixWare; SCO Enterprise; IBM OS/2 SMP; 
Banyan VINES; and Digital PATHWORKS.

     The Prioris HX 5133 is covered by a three-year, on-site limited 
warranty, with next-business day response standard from Digital's 
Multivendor Customer Services organization or an authorized Digital 
channel partner.  Digital's full line of Prioris PC servers deliver 
maximum investment longevity through balanced system design and 
robust fault-tolerance.

Configuration and Availability

     Several configurations are available, including a base-level 
Prioris HX 5133 server with one 133MHz Pentium processor, 16MB of 
parity memory, and a PCI Fast-Wide SCSI-2 adapter.  A Prioris HX 
5133DP server includes two 133MHz Pentium processors, 32MB of 
memory, and a PCI Fast-Wide SCSI-2 adapter.  A RAID-based Prioris HX 
5133 system includes one 133MHz Pentium processor, 16MB of parity 
memory, a high-performance, dual-channel PCI RAID controller and two 
hot-swap Fast-Wide (7200) SCSI-2, 2GB drives.  One RAID-based 
Prioris HX 5133DP configuration includes two 133MHz Pentium 
processors, 32MB of ECC memory, a high-performance, dual-channel PCI 
RAID controller and four hot-swap Fast-Wide (7200) SCSI-2, 2GB 
drives.  All models come standard with 512KB write-back cache, dual 
speed SCSI CD-ROM drive, and a keyboard, mouse and floppy disk 
drive.  The U.S. list price for a base configuration Prioris HX 5133 
system starts at $6,999.  The dual-processor base configuration 
starts at $12,999. 

     The systems are available through Digital's channel partners, 
including master resellers, wholesalers, distributors, dealers, VARs 
and system integrators, as well as Digital's direct sales 
organization.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
