            DIGITAL STORAGE PRODUCT WINS INDUSTRY AWARDS


       StorageWorks RAID Array 230 Selected "Best Product" in
       BYTE Magazine and PC Digest RAID Array Product Reviews


MAYNARD, Mass. -- October 5, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced its StorageWorks RAID Array 230 subsystem received 
"Best Overall Product" awards from two influential industry 
publications.  Introduced in July, the RAID Array 230 topped 16 
competing RAID subsystems tested by National Software Testing 
Laboratories (NSTL) for head-to-head product comparisons in the 
September 1995 issue of BYTE Magazine and in the July 1995 issue of 
PC Digest, (volume 9, number 7).

     The September BYTE Magazine named the StorageWorks RAID Array 
230 "Best Overall Product," "Best for Database Servers," and "Best 
for Audio/Video." In the "Overall Product" category, the RAID Array 
230 received top scores in a range of critical areas, including 
optimum performance, breadth of features and ease of use, topping 
solutions from Clariion Advanced Storage, Conner Storage Systems, 
StorageTek Distributed Systems Division, and others.  In the 
"Database Server" category, benchmark scores were analyzed, and the 
RAID Array 230 was determined to have the best performance among the 
16 arrays. In the "Audio/Video" category, the RAID Array 230 
received the highest overall ranking when using disk storage for 
audio/video applications. 

     "The Digital StorageWorks RAID Array 230 Subsystem was the 
clear overall winner in our testing.  Its fast performance and wide 
range of features, including redundant and hot-swappable drives, 
power supplies, fans, a sixth drive for a hot spare, and a write 
cache with battery backup, placed it well above the other subsystems 
tested," wrote Michele Guy, NSTL Project Manager. "The StorageWorks 
RAID Array 230 is also one of the least expensive units we tested."

     In addition, the July PC Digest rated the StorageWorks RAID 
Array 230 number one, awarding the product four stars out of a 
possible five with top ratings in performance, features and 
usability.

StorageWorks RAID Array 230 

     The StorageWorks RAID Array 230, a competitively-priced PCI 
RAID solution for PC networks, is designed for Intel systems running 
Novell NetWare 3.12/4.1 or Microsoft Windows NT V3.5.  A hardware-
based disk array, the RAID Array 230 provides expandable, cost-
effective storage for RAID levels 0, 1, 0+1, 5, and JBOD (just a 
bunch of disks) and supports both 8-bit and 16-bit drives.  With a 
4MB FastCache (expandable to 32MB), the array is optimized for fast 
read-write operations.  The RAID Array 230 provides continuous 
access to data via automatic, unattended rebuilds and hot spare/hot 
swap disk drive configurations.  The StorageWorks RAID Array 230 
Subsystem is priced starting at $6,935 and consists of a 
StorageWorks PCI backplane hardware RAID controller, RAID 
configuration and management utilities software, redundant power 
supplies, and three 1.05GB disk drives with the appropriate cables 
and enclosure.  For more information about Digital's complete line 
of StorageWorks products, call 1-800-STORWORK (1-800-786-7967).

     The StorageWorks product line is a comprehensive family of 
disk, tape, and optical storage subsystems, offering modular, 
competitively-priced, industry-standard solutions in customizable 
desktop, deskside, departmental, and datacenter enclosures.  
StorageWorks products are available on multiple operating systems 
and hardware platforms, including Digital workstations, systems and 
servers; Novell and Windows NT environments; and Hewlett-Packard, 
IBM, and Sun workstations and servers.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
